# The usage report is PASSWORD PROTECTED and is the only thing in this directory.
#
# Tom, 2026-09-17: *"I'm feeling a bit private at the moment, so password protection might be
# nice."* HTTP Basic is what answers that without storing anything of ours on anybody's device:
# the browser holds the credential, there is no session, no cookie and no consent question, and
# the suite's session count stays at zero (Task 288).
#
# THIS FILE IS WHY THE PAGE HAS A DIRECTORY OF ITS OWN. AuthType and friends need
# `AllowOverride AuthConfig`, which is a SEPARATE grant from the FileInfo/Limit the root
# .htaccess relies on. Where it is not granted Apache returns 500 for every request in the
# directory holding the file -- the same trap the root .htaccess records about `Options
# -Indexes`, which needs `AllowOverride Options` and 500s the whole suite where that is missing.
# Down here the blast radius is this page and nothing else, and it fails CLOSED.
#
# AuthUserFile MUST BE AN ABSOLUTE PATH ON THE SERVER and must be somewhere the web cannot
# reach, so it is outside the document root on purpose. If the password file is absent Apache
# answers 500 for this directory: that is also fail-closed, and it is the state this ships in
# until the file is made. dev/usage-report-page.md has the three commands that make it.
AuthType Basic
AuthName "EngCalcs usage report"
AuthUserFile /home/jconstru/.htpasswd-engcalcs
Require valid-user

# Belt and braces on the search engines, since a 401 is not itself a promise of non-indexing and
# the page also carries a robots meta.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
    Header set X-Robots-Tag "noindex, nofollow"
</IfModule>
